From cb468df1a521f4f5b93c24c9b6a2e1e8fd338f1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:15:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Solvers of Trilinos: eighth review

- In the iterative mode, the multigrids, relaxations and direct solvers of
  Trilinos correct the initial guess from its residual, as BoomerAMG of
  hypre does: MueLu used as an approximate linear solver overwrote it.
  The test checks that the stationary iteration with one V-cycle of
  MueLu converges (relative residual 2e-15 after 30 iterations, against
  0.07 to 0.17 for one V-cycle).
- The test checks one V-cycle of MueLu as a linear solver, and that the
  factories written with Kokkos reduce the iterations.
- The UUIDs of the GPUs are exchanged as bytes.
- Comments and documentation: UUIDs instead of PCI addresses, row of
  MueLu in the table of the linear solvers, glossary, linear solver of
  the elastic operator, aggregation order of the factories which are not
  written with Kokkos, options of the factories written with Kokkos named
  in full.
